    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll analyze the existing code to understand the bulk-approve implementation and then add the bulk-reject Action following the same patterns.\n\nNow I understand the structure. Let me check the SCHEMA.sql to understand the tables:\n\nNow I understand the complete picture. I need to:\n\n1. Add a `Reject` transition in `internal/action/action.go` (but this file is protected - I need to declare it in `internal/candidate`)\n2. Add the `reject` handler in `internal/candidate/approval.go`\n3. Register the `/purchases/bulk-reject` route in `internal/protocol/protocol.go`\n\nWait, I need to re-read the task. It says \"Only edit/add internal/candidate/ Go code\" and \"Declare any new Transition value in internal/candidate\". So I should add the transition declaration in the candidate package, not in the protected action package.\n\nLet me create the reject transition in `internal/candidate/approval.go` and update the files accordingly:\n\nNow let me verify the code compiles:\n\nBuild and tests pass. Let me verify the implementation is complete by reviewing the modified file:\n\nDone. I've added the `POST /purchases/bulk-reject` endpoint to the existing service:\n\n**Changes made to `internal/candidate/approval.go`:**\n\n1. Added `Reject` transition declaration with operation `\"bulk-reject.v4\"`, from `\"submitted\"` to `\"rejected\"`, field `\"rejectedIds\"`\n\n2. Added `reject` handler that:\n   - Calls the Action kernel with `Reject` transition\n   - Sorts returned IDs by UTF-8 dictionary order\n   - Returns proper protocol.Result\n\n3. Registered `/purchases/bulk-reject` route in the Routes map alongside `/purchases/bulk-approve`\n\n**Key behaviors implemented:**\n- Only authenticated approvers can reject purchases\n- Only rejected submitted purchases in the same tenant (not self-created) are eligible\n- Full idempotency support via the shared Action kernel (same key+identity+target set = replay)\n- 409 conflict for ineligible targets or key collisions\n- 503 on ActionRequest write failure\n- All existing bulk-approve behavior preserved\n- Response contains only `rejectedIds` sorted in UTF-8 order"
